{{also|go ahead}}
==English==

===Etymology===
As a name for footwear, from the fact that one can't easily step backwards wearing them.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[go]]-[[ahead]]}}

# [[approval|Approval]], [[agreement]], or [[instruction]] to begin or [[proceed]].
#: {{ux|en|You can start as soon as you get the '''go-ahead''' from the president.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 June 3|author=Lilian Greenwood talks to Paul Stephen|title=Rail's 'underlying challenges' remain|journal=Rail|page=34|text=Greenwood's time as TSC <small>[Transport Select Committee]</small> chairman came to an end late last year, when MPs finally gave the '''go-ahead''' to an early General Election so that the Brexit deadlock in Parliament could be broken.}}
# {{lb|en|dated|usually plural}} [[flip-flop]]

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|head=[[go]]-[[ahead]]}}

# {{lb|en|comparable}} [[progressive|Progressive]]; exerting leadership.
#: ''I work for a very '''go-ahead''' company that's always looking for new ideas.''
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1906|author=Arthur Lincoln Haydon|title=The Book of the V. C.|page=150|passage=This turbulent ruler was a very '''go-ahead''' monarch indeed. He organised a splendid army, well-drilled and well-equipped with modern arms}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1959|year_published=1972|author=Anthony Burgess|authorlink=Anthony Burgess|title=Beds in the East|series=The Malayan Trilogy|page=587|passage="The Sultan's '''go-ahead''', modern in some of his views."}}
# {{lb|en|comparable}} [[dashing|Dashing]]; [[energetic]].
# {{lb|en|sports|not comparable}} Being a [[score]] which gives the scoring team or player the lead in the game.
#: ''The pitcher gave up the '''go-ahead''' run in the top of the ninth inning.''

